If you have an __init__.py  you are sure to go through, you can add the following code to your file:

{code}
# PySpark adds a SIGCHLD signal handler, but that breaks other packages, so we remove it
try:
    import signal
    signal.signal(signal.SIGCHLD, signal.SIG_DFL)
except: pass
{code}

It's a work around, it would be better to have a "smart" signal handler that only handles the processes that are direct descendants of the daemon. I might try to get something like that out.

