Current situation: 
1. The TimeoutException is thrown by ReliableKafkaReceiver, receiver logs the error and do nothing else;
2. Block pushing thread in BlockGenerator is terminated due to the exception;
3. ReliableKafkaReceiver is ACTIVE but rogues afterward because blocksForPushing queue is full and no block pushing thread available to clean the queue.

So when the exception occurs, what user will see is the streaming application keeps running but sits there doing nothing (We are using some supervisor to restart the failed app. But if the app keeps running and doing nothing, we have to have some curator to monitor the data flow and kill the app in such situation). Can ReliableKafkaReceiver handle TimeoutException? For example retry pushing block when a TimeoutException is thrown? Or restart itself? Or at least fail the streaming application?

